SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/lib/mh:$PATH
# MAILDIR set to Mail folder and this is the default
MAILDIR=$HOME/Mail
DEFAULT=$MAILDIR/
LOGFILE=$HOME/Mail/logfile
SENDMAIL=/usr/sbin/sendmail
# Ensures log file has detailed logging
VERBOSE=1

# Recipe 1: Checks and catches any messages that have multiple addresses in the From: header (catches junkMail 1-50)
# :0: ensures that a similar message isn't sent to the mailbox.
# H flag checks header only 
:0 H:
* ^From:.*@.*,
recipe1

# Recipe 2: Checks Subject: for keywords that suggest that the message is spam (catches junkMail 51-63)
# I flag ensures case-insensitivity
# \bED\b uses word boundaries to match only a whole word
# v.?a.?g.?r pattern catches when viagara is mispelled in the text
# bb[a-z]*y does something similar but for buy
# impot and imphotgnce are for mispellings of impotence  
:0 HI:
* ^Subject:.*(\bED\b|diploma|degree|college|medications|potency|pills|cheap|guaranteed|bb[a-z]*y|v.?a.?g.?r|impot|imphotgence|Inteveo)
recipe2

# Recipe 3: Checks the Body content for spam, body checking is done with B flag (catches junkMail 64-66)
# The Ruby Palace checks for casino spam
# Sub-Penny and G_GSM check for stock pump-and-dump spam
:0 BI:
* (Ruby Palace|Sub-Penny|G_GSM)
recipe3

# Recipe 4: Checks header and body for compound rules to catch spam -- HB flag -- (catches junkMail 67-74)
# Need both checks together to pass since neither is specific enough to actually catch spam (could accidentally flag the wrong thing)
# Condition 1: multipart/alternative means email has both plaintext and HTML versions which is aa common format for bulk/spam mailers.
# Condition 2: https?://, this one matches any http:// or https:// URL in the body.
:0 HB:
* ^Content-Type: multipart/alternative
* https?://
recipe4

## Below are the recipes that were already in the procmailrc file...

## Recipe_1:
##
:0 :
* ^From.*purdue\.edu
* ^Subject.*404
my404Folder

## Recipe_2:
##
## This recipe will only be invoked if the subject line
## constains the string 'sports' This email will go into
## your mailbox for the special account.  You need to
## replace the 'your_special_account_name' string with what
## applies to you
##
:0 :
* ^Subject.*sports
/var/mail/ece404b5

## Recipe_3:
##
## This is an emailing recipe.  It will send to your regular
## Purdue webmail account all messages that originate from
## the purdue.edu domain and that have survived the previous
## recipes.
##
##
## IMPORTANT NOTE: The email address in the last line of the
## recipe is your Purdue webmail address --- the address on
## which you normally receive your email DO NOT put your
## special account name in that line since that would create
## an infinite loop.
##
:0 :
* ^From.*(purdue\.edu[ ]|purdue\.edu>)
!pboredd@purdue.edu

## Recipe_4:
##
## This is one of the recipes in your instructor's spam
## filter. If your drug related spam does not originate from
## Purdue, this recipe will kick in.  
##
## IMPORTANT: Since spammers fake their headers, a spam
## message actually coming from outside Purdue may still
## look like it is coming from Purdue.
##
:0 B
* < 10000
* (\<v.codin\>|\<viicodin\>|\<vi.?c0[^a-z]din\>|\<vi.?codin.?\>|v[^a-z]codin|\<..?a1ium\>|\<val.?iu.?m\>|\<v@[^a-z]ium\>|\<vi0xx\>|va-[^a-z]ium|\<va1[ ]?[ ]?ium\>|\<valliuum\>|\<pr.ozac\>|\<vall.um\>|\<amb.jen\>|\<ui.tram\>|\<pro.zac\>|\<val..um\>|\<val...um\>|\<pr...zac\>|>mbie.n|\<v a l|\<va..um\>|\<v.alium\>|\<va.llum\>|\<va.ll.?um\>|\<va.lium\>|\<vali.um\>|\<przoac|\<levtira|\<zolotf|lorazpeam|prozaac)
* (\<vi.gra\>|\<v1a[^a-z]gra\>|[^a-z]/iaa?gra\>|\<vii?aa?graa?|\<v[^a-z]agra\>|\<via[ ][ ]?gra\>|\<vi[ ]+graa?|\<v..agra\>|\<v.agg?ra\>|\<v.agr..a|>i.agra|g r a|v i a|\<vi..ra\>|\<v.iagra\>|\<v..agra\>|\<v..agra\>|\<viag.ra\>|\<vaigra|\<vair.a\>|\<vai..ra\>|\<vai.?gra\>)
* (\<cialli.s\>|\<cia[^a-z]ii?s\>|\<cia[ ]?[ ]?1is\>|\<cia.?l.?is\>|\<cai[ ]+llis\>|\<xa.?naa?x\>|\<xan[ ]?ax\>|\<x[^a-z]an@x\>|\<meds\>|\<[0-9]o-?%|codeinn?e|\<c..alis\>|\<xa.nax\>|\<c.all.s\>|\<xan...ax\>|a.nax\>|i.alis\>|a l [it] s|c [it] a l|c / a|l / s|\<ci...lis\>|\<c.ialis\>|\<ci.alls\>|\<c..al.s\>|\<cial.is\>|\<cailis|\<caillis|\<xnaax|\<ca.ilis\>)
* (http://|\<www\>)
{
  LOG="Email Trashed by Recipe_4$EOL"

  :0 :
  /dev/null
}

## Recipe_5:
##
## This is another recipe from your instructor's spam filter
##
:0 HB
* charset="koi8-r"
{
  LOG="Email trashed because it is in Russian$EOL"

  :0 :
  /dev/null
}

# This line catches any messages that were not matched by the above recipes and sends them to an uncaught file in the mail directory
:0:
$MAILDIR/uncaught

## Recipe_6:
## 
## The rest of the email to your special account will be 
## deposited in the file spamFolder
##
:0 :
spamFolder